$DATUM 1-(2-Morpholinoethyl)-3-(3-(naphthalen-1-yloxy)propyl)-7-(o-tolyl)-1H-indole-2-carboxylic
Acid (14). To a solution of bromide 13 (0.07 g, 0.124 mmol),
o-tolylboronic acid (0.052 g, 0.382 mmol), and
dichlorobis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(II) (0.001 g, 1.425 μmol) in
DME/EtOH/H2O (7:3:2) (3 mL) was added LiOH· H2O (0.05 g, 2.088 mmol). The
reaction was heated to 150 °C for 30 min in a Biotage initiator microwave
reactor. EtOAc was added. The reaction was filtered through a drying
cartridge (MgSO4, Alltech Associates, 2 g) and concentrated. The residue
was purified by reverse phase preparative HPLC. 0.058 g (85%) of the
title compound. 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 8.21-8.25 (m, 1H), 7.86-7.90
(m, 1H), 7.79-7.83 (m, 1H), 7.49-7.57 (m, 2H), 7.30-7.48 (m, 6H), 7.15
(t, J =7.63 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (d, J = 7.02 Hz, 1H), 6.91 (d, J = 7.63 Hz,
1H), 4.58-4.73 (m, 2H), 4.23 (t, J = 6.10 Hz, 2H), 3.95-4.08 (m, 2H),
3.46-3.73 (m, 4H), 2.55-2.80 (m, 4H), 2.19-2.27 (m, 2H), 2.00 (s, 3H). MS
(ESI) m/z = 549.4 (M + H+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure-Guided Design of a Series of MCL-1 Inhibitors with High
Affinity and Selectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
