$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the Suzuki coupling on the 3,9-diiodo-7H-benzo[
de]anthracen-7-one (19) 3,9-diiodo-7H-benzo[de]anthracen-7-one (19) (0.48
g, 1.0 mmol), aryl boronic acid (2.5 mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (30 mg), PPh3
(20 mg), potassium carbonate (1.38 g, 10.0 mmol) were taken in a mixture
of toluene (50 ml) and water (10 ml). Reaction mixture was heated at 110
ºC for 5 h in nitrogen atmosphere. On completion of reaction, reaction
mixture was cooled and toluene layer was separated. Toluene was removed
under vacuum, and product was purified by column chromatography using
dichloromethane/hexane as eluent to afford product. Preparation of
3,9-diphenyl-7H-benzo[de]anthracen-7-one (20) According to general
reaction procedure, 3,9-diiodo-7H-benzo[de]anthracen-7-one (19) and
phenylboronic acid (0.26 g, 2.5 mmol) were reacted. Product as yellow
powder. Yield: 0.29 g, 77%. Mp: 180 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ:
8.84-8.78 (m, 2H), 8.52 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 8.44 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H),
8.32 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 8.01 (dd, J = 9.6, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.80-7.72 (m,
3H), 7.66 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.56-7.50 (m, 7H), 7.42 (t, J = 7.2 Hz,
1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ: 183.9, 142.7, 140.7, 139.7, 139.6,
134.9, 133.6, 131.7, 131.3, 131.1, 130.2, 129.8, 128.9, 128.7, 128.4,
128.1, 127.9, 127.8, 127.5, 128.0, 126.5, 126.1, 125.8, 125.7, 123.7.
MALDI-TOF MS: calculated for [C29H18O]+: 382.1385, found: 382.1370.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
