$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure To Synthesize Compounds of
Formula 9. 3-(6-Chloro-5-(E)-styrylpyridin-3-yl)pyridine. To a reaction
vessel in a nitrogen atmosphere containing
5-bromo-2-chloro-3-(E)-styrylpyridine (5; 1.5 g, 5.08 mmol) were added
pyridin-3-yl boronic acid (781 mg, 6.35 mmol),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (5% mol), and Na2CO3 (2.5 equiv)
in 1,4-dioxane. The mixture was stirred at reflux for 24 h, followed by
TLC. The product was cooled to room temperature and filtered on Celite.
The solution was dried on MgSO4, filtered, and evaporated. The residue
was purified by chromatography (c-hexane/ ethylacetate= 7:3),
2-Chloro-5-phenyl-3-(E)-styrylpyridine. The general procedure was
followed using phenyl boronic acid (929 mg, 7.62 mmol) and
5-bromo-2-chloro-3-(E)-styrylpyridine (5; 1.5 g, 5.08 mmol). The residue
was purified by chromatography (c-hexane/ethyl acetate = 9:1), The title
compound (1.10 g) as a colorless oil (yield 74%). IR (KBr disc): 3058,
3033, 2924, 2850, 1630, 1601, 1580, 1546, 1494, 1448, 1417, 1407, 1390,
1322, 1222, 1210, 1162, 1116, 1085, 1054, 1008, 961, 903, 845, 762, 741,
696, 563 cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 8.54 (d, 1H, J = 2.4 Hz), 8, 07 (d, 1H,
J = 2.4 Hz), 7.59-7.24 (m, 11H), 7.11 (d, 1H, J = 16 Hz, CH=CH). 13C NMR
(CDCl3): δ 146.3, 143.8, 136.4, 135.3, 135.2, 134.6, 133.4, 132.5, 129.3
(2C), 128.8, 128.7 (2C), 128, 127.5 (2C), 127.4, 126.4 (2C). LCMS(EI):
292.35 [M + H+], 294.34 [M+ + 2].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
