$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for N-Boc-Protected o-Aryl
Anilines. A mixture of N-Boc-protected o-bromoaniline 1 (1 equiv), the
corresponding boronic acid (1.6 equiv),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium (5 mol %), and potassium carbonate
(2.5 equiv) in toluene/ EtOH (4/1) (0.1 M) was stirred at 80 °C under an
argon atmosphere for 2-4 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with AcOEt,
washed with water and brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(hexanes/AcOEt) to afford the desired product. tert-Butyl
3-(2-((tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino)-4-methylphenyl)-1H-pyrrole-1-carboxylate.
The product was obtained following the general procedure (3.0 mmol scale)
as an amorphous solid (805 mg, 72%) after purification by column
chromatography. Rf = 0.35 (5% AcOEt/hexanes); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.91 (br
s, 1H), 7.35 (br s, 1H), 7.30 (br s, 1H), 7.14 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 6.87
(d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 6.75 (br s, 1H), 6.33 (dd, J = 3.2, 1.7 Hz, 1H),
2.37 (s, 3H), 1.62 (s, 9H), 1.51 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 153.0, 148.6,
138.1, 135.4, 129.5, 124.0, 123.8, 121.5, 121.0, 120.2, 117.9, 112.7,
84.1, 80.3, 28.3, 28.0, 21.5; IR (neat) 3418, 2980, 1728, 1522, 1387,
1344 cm-1; MS (FAB) m/z 372 (M+), 316 (M -t-Bu), 260 (M -2t-Bu), 173 (M
-2Boc); HRMS-ESI (m/z) calcd for C21H28KN2O4 411.1686, found 411.1692.
